    {
      "id": "claim_6ae27ef5450f44fab921f7e1e98da446",
      "statement": "Application-layer encryption is optional and off by default (DEFAULT_SEND_OPTIONS.isEncrypt false): when enabled, each file gets its own AES-256-GCM key wrapped with the receiver's RSA-OAEP-2048 public key, with the wrapped key delivered inside the metaData message, protecting file content from SDP-exchange MITM on top of DTLS; the answer peer awaits the validated p-param import before generating its own RSA pair for the answer code, and the offer side tracks the effective session encryption in a plain $state effectiveEncrypt that onOptionsUpdate re-syncs on every sendOptions change (the downgrade branch may override it to false for the current handshake).",
